\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. I've found a Friend; O such a Friend!
\par He loved me ere I knew Him;
\par He drew me with the cords of love,
\par And thus He bound me to Him;
\par And round my heart still closely twine
\par Those ties which nought can sever;
\par For I am His, and He is mine,
\par For ever and for ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. I've found a Friend; O such a Friend!
\par He bled, He died to save me;
\par And not alone the gift of life,
\par But His own self He gave me.
\par Nought that I have mine own I call,
\par I hold it for the Giver,
\par My heart, my strength, my life, my all,
\par Are His, and His for ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. I've found a Friend; O such a Friend!
\par All power to Him is given,
\par To guard me on my onward course
\par And bring me safe to heaven.
\par Eternal glories gleam afar,
\par To nerve my faint endeavour;
\par So now to watch, to work, to war,
\par And then to rest for ever.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. I've found a Friend; O such a Friend!
\par So kind, and true, and tender!
\par So wise a Counsellor and Guide,
\par So mighty a Defender!
\par From Him who loves me now so well
\par What power my soul shall sever?
\par Shall life or death? shall earth or hell?
\par No! I am His for ever.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

